<title>CROATIA: Croatian oil, natural gas output rises in July.</title>
<headline>Croatian oil, natural gas output rises in July.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Central Bureau of Statistics issued the following oil and natural gas output figures.</p>
<p>					JULY	 JUNE	 JULY '95</p>
<p> Crude oil (tonnes)	    117,746    108,530     126,453</p>
<p> Natural gas (thousand cu m) 139,354    111,580     170,375</p>
<p> Gasoline			  113,984     88,825     134,745</p>
<p> Gas oil			    73,204     89,032     107,137</p>
<p> Heating oil		     134,111    158,781     147,279</p>
<p>NOTE -- Data exclude production in Serb-held Eastern Slavonia, an area due to revert to government control, where output from some oilfields was restarted by national oil company INA late in August. -- Kolumbina Bencevic, Zagreb Newsroom, +385-1-4557075</p>
</text>
